          "snippet": "Early phenomenologists advanced a metaphysical realist and essentialist ontology characterized by the distinction between objects and states of affairs. This framework sparked debate regarding whether all meaningful sentences refer to ontologically independent states of affairs, with Reinach arguing for their universal existence while Daubert proposed that cognized states of affairs depend on mental acts."
        },
