          "snippet": "Nozick argues that historical entitlement principles, grounded in property rights and self-ownership, are superior to end-state or patterned theories of distributive justice. He contends that maintaining any distributional pattern inevitably requires continuous interference with individuals' voluntary choices, thereby violating their liberty. Furthermore, he asserts that redistributive measures undermine the very justice of initial holdings by rescinding an individual's right to dispose of their possessions as they see fit."
