          "snippet": "John Rawls develops the original position as a hypothetical device to establish impartial principles of justice, grounding his theory in Kantian constructivism where objectivity arises from a procedure of construction rather than pre-existing moral facts. This framework employs constraints like the veil of ignorance and publicity to ensure fairness, aiming for reflective equilibrium between considered convictions and theoretical principles despite various philosophical objections regarding its determinacy and relevance."
