          "snippet": "Immanuel Kant argues that causality and other fundamental scientific principles are a priori categories of the understanding rather than empirical generalizations derived from Humean custom. By positing these transcendental concepts, he claims to resolve Hume's skepticism by grounding objective necessity and strict universality in the structure of human cognition instead of mere induction or subjective association."
        },
