          "score": 0.6729788,
          "snippet": "Kant argues that the concept of causality involves a necessary connection and strict universality, which cannot be derived empirically from repeated observations or constant conjunctions as Hume suggested. Instead, this a priori principle transforms subjective temporal sequences into objective events by positing that every effect follows necessarily from its cause according to universal rules."
        },
